<title>UK: Alliance &amp; Leicester sets flotation date.</title>
<headline>Alliance &amp; Leicester sets flotation date.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Alliance &amp; Leicester Building Society said on Monday it had set April 21 provisionally as the date for its planned flotation as part of its conversion to a public limited company.</p>
<p>Alliance &amp; Leicester said the final timetable would depend on regulators and market conditions. It said it had not yet decided on a final qualifying date for its members to be eligible for free shares.</p>
<p>Several British building societies have opted to shed their mutual status and go public. Customers have benefited from share handouts as part of that process.</p>
</text>
